Configure relationships:
Each relationship has a single "from" column and a single "to" column. It's important that the data types for these columns are the same (or equivalent) and that they contain matching values.
If data source has a multi-column key,then need to transform the data to produce single-column keys for the related tables.
For One-to-one cardinality,best practice is to use Power Query to merge queries to produce a single model table.
Cross-filter direction determines how filters propagate.
There can only be one active filter propagation path between two model tables. 
The Synonyms property allows you to set one or more alternative names for the table
The Auto date/time feature in Power BI automatically creates hidden date tables for each date column in your data model.
Time Intelligence Generates 
>.A calculated table using the CALENDAR function for each date column
>.Adds columns like Year, Quarter, Month, Day to support drill-downs and filtering
>.Creates a hierarchy (Year → Quarter → Month → Day) for visuals
>.Automatically links the hidden date table to your original date column
